       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled metformin dose. The limit is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nCould this be a typo? Some common regimens are:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **500 mg PO three times daily with meals** (1,500 mg/day)\n- **1000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **1700 mg/day total**, which might have been meant as a daily total and not a per-dose amount (for example, 850 mg twice daily)\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you really do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that and give a clinical rationale. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
